  "title": "Adverbs, conjunctions, prepositions and interjections",
  "lesson": {
    "kind": "deepen",
    "focusPoint": 2,
    "points": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "heading": "Point 1: Review of the last class",
        "body": "What did you learn in the last class?\n\nLast class you studied nouns, verbs, pronouns, articles and adjectives. Today we finish the team on Mount Ávila."
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "heading": "Point 2: An adverb tells how",
        "body": "The team climbs Mount Ávila. How do you say that they climb without hurry?\n\nYou say: “The team climbs slowly.” “Slowly” is an adverb (adverbio). It tells how. Others tell when: “today”."
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "heading": "Point 3: A conjunction joins ideas",
        "body": "Join “I climb” and “I am tired”. Which small word goes in the middle?\n\nYou say: “I climb, but I am tired.” “But” is a conjunction (conjunción). “And” adds and “or” gives a choice."
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "heading": "Point 4: A preposition links words",
        "body": "Fill in: “Sofia climbs ___ her friend.” What changes with “with”? And “without”?\n\n“With her friend”: they climb together. “Without her friend”: Sofia climbs alone. “With” is a preposition (preposición)."
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "heading": "Point 5: An interjection shows feeling",
        "body": "You reach the top of Mount Ávila. What do you shout when you feel happy?\n\nYou can shout “Wow!” or “Yay!” They are interjections (interjecciones): they show a feeling right away."
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "heading": "Point 6: Tell it in order",
        "body": "Back home, you tell your family about the nine groups. How do you order it?\n\nFirst say hello. Then name the groups: noun, pronoun, verb, adjective, adverb, preposition, conjunction, interjection, and the articles a, an, the: 9 groups. Last, say thank you."
      }
    ],
    "summary": "Adverbs, conjunctions, prepositions and interjections complete the nine groups, and you can tell them in order.",
